;; clj-kondo export for day8/re-frame2-hicasso (rf2-hic-022).
;;
;; A consumer picks this up with clj-kondo's ordinary dependency import —
;; nothing here is re-frame2-specific plumbing:
;;
;;   clj-kondo --lint "$(clojure -Spath)" --dependencies --copy-configs
;;
;; which copies this directory to `.clj-kondo/day8/re-frame2-hicasso/` and
;; adds it to the consumer's `:config-paths`. See README.md beside this file
;; for what each check knows, and — the more useful half — what it refuses to
;; know.
;;
;; SEVERITY LAW (operator ruling, rf2-hic-022, 2026-08-10): ERRORS only for
;; TRUE INVARIANTS; WARNINGS for heuristics; nothing blocks a build.
;; Assistance, not enforcement.
;;
;; So two errors, and they are the two forms that are wrong under every
;; circumstance and that the runtime itself refuses: a view called like a
;; function, and a function where a hiccup head belongs. The rest are advice,
;; and a warning cannot red the repo's own gate either — `clj-kondo` runs
;; `--fail-level error`, so items 3-5 are advisory by construction.
;;
;; The `:&`-carrying-a-non-map check was here and is GONE: the `:&` grammar key
;; is retired from the end-state design in favour of the owned-wins merge
;; recipe, and a lint layer must not police a ghost.
;;
;; Every level is a consumer's to change, and turning one off is a supported
;; answer:
;;
;;   {:linters {:re-frame.hicasso/unkeyed-mapped-child {:level :off}}}
{:linters
 {:re-frame.hicasso/direct-view-call               {:level :error}
  :re-frame.hicasso/function-in-head-position      {:level :error}
  :re-frame.hicasso/deferred-read                  {:level :warning}
  :re-frame.hicasso/unkeyed-mapped-child           {:level :warning}
  :re-frame.hicasso/nameless-interactive-element   {:level :warning}
  :re-frame.hicasso/parked-read                    {:level :warning}}

 ;; The native tier's defining macro (rf2-hic-030). `defcomponent` is
 ;; `defn`-shaped ALREADY — `(defcomponent sym doc? decl-map? [argv] body+)`
 ;; is exactly `clojure.core/defn`'s `name doc-string? attr-map? [params*]
 ;; body` — so it needs a rewrite rather than a hook: nothing about the
 ;; native tier is checkable beyond the var it defines and the body it
 ;; carries, and inventing a check here would be the lint layer growing a
 ;; semantics the runtime does not have.
 ;;
 ;; `n/$` and `n/props` deliberately get NOTHING. They are ordinary macro
 ;; calls whose operands are ordinary expressions, so clj-kondo already
 ;; reads them correctly; a hook that re-stated the grammar would be a
 ;; second, drifting copy of the one in `re-frame.hicasso.native`.
 :lint-as
 {re-frame.hicasso.native/defcomponent clojure.core/defn}

 :hooks
 {:analyze-call
  {re-frame.hicasso/defview hooks.re-frame.hicasso/defview
   re-frame.hicasso/hfn     hooks.re-frame.hicasso/hfn
   re-frame.hicasso/defhost hooks.re-frame.hicasso/defhost}}}
